---
// High pressure cleaning (HOMES) — a LEAF page under the Home Cleaning
// mega-menu's third group, "Outside your home" (navigation.ts).
//
// ⚠️ THIS PAGE HAS A COMMERCIAL TWIN, and that page's source asked for this
// comment. /commercial-cleaning/commercial-pressure-cleaning/ sits under the Commercial menu and
// was built first. The two will compete for the same queries unless they stay
// in their lanes:
//   - THAT page is workplaces: car parks, loading docks, bin bays, trading
//     hours, WHS duties and wash water compliance. Its reader is responsible
//     for premises.
//   - THIS page is homes: driveways, paths, patios, pool surrounds, fences and
//     retaining walls. Its reader lives there.
// Deliberate differences that keep them apart: the language ("your place", not
// "the site", per BFD 2.3), the CTA (an instant quote, not a site
// walkthrough), the surfaces, and the fact that this page spends its warning
// on what NOT to pressure clean around a house, which a car park does not
// have. Each links to the other so a misrouted visitor has somewhere to go.
//
// NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS for any of the five in this group. All copy below is
// DRAFTED, not supplied, and needs sign-off. Facts only TLB holds ship as
// visible [brackets].
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH (the first four are shared with the commercial twin, and one
// answer fixes both pages):
//   - IS THIS DELIVERED IN HOUSE? Pressure cleaning needs its own plant: a
//     petrol unit, a rotary surface cleaner, hose and in many cases a water
//     tank. If it is subcontracted, §9's comparison table ("employed by TLB,
//     not subcontracted") contradicts the page and comes off it.
//   - HOT WATER OR COLD? §5 says oil and grease need heat or a degreaser with
//     dwell time. If TLB runs cold only, cut the grease claims.
//   - WATER SUPPLY AND POWER. Branded FAQ 4 is bracketed. It is the third
//     question every caller asks.
//   - PRICING BASIS and minimum charge. Bracketed in non-branded FAQ 5.
//   - DO WE DO TIMBER DECKS? §4's warning says a deck needs a different
//     approach, not a blast. Confirm whether TLB takes deck work at all,
//     because half the enquiries from this page will ask.
//   - RETAINING WALLS, FENCES AND POOL SURROUNDS are named in §6's list.
//     Confirm each one.
//   - [insured] in §3 card 3 is inherited from the commercial hub.
//
// PHOTOGRAPHY: four generated assets of its own in
// src/assets/home_cleaning/outside_your_home/high_pressure_cleaning/, prompts
// in the IMAGE-PROMPTS.md beside them, plus the cluster's shared backdrop one
// level up. NOTHING is reused from the commercial pressure folder: those four
// frames are a commercial forecourt and a shopfront, and IMAGE-GUIDELINES §5
// forbids relabelling a photo to mean something it does not show.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/sections/SiteHeader.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../components/sections/TrustBar.astro';
import Backdrop from '../../components/ui/Backdrop.astro';
import TextBlock from '../../components/sections/TextBlock.astro';
import PathwayCards from '../../components/sections/PathwayCards.astro';
import ServiceBlocks from '../../components/sections/ServiceBlocks.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/sections/Callout.astro';
import BeforeAfter from '../../components/sections/BeforeAfter.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/sections/ComparisonTable.astro';
import GoogleReviewSlider from '../../components/sections/GoogleReviewSlider.astro';
import { googleBusinessProfileUrl, googleReviews } from '../../data/googleReviews';
import TagCloud from '../../components/sections/TagCloud.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/sections/Faq.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/sections/CallToAction.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/sections/SiteFooter.astro';
import logoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-horizontal.png';
import footerLogoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-square.png';
// Shared across all five pages in this group. See the window page's note.
// SAMPLE illustrations, not photographs. See §7.
import {
  primaryNav,
  headerNav,
  headerSecondaryCta,
  footerServiceLinks,
  footerContact,
  footerCopyright,
  quoteCta,
} from '../../data/navigation';
import { comparisonColumns, comparisonRows } from '../../data/comparison';
import { locationGroups } from '../../data/locations';
import { trustBarCards } from '../../data/trust';
import { otherOutsideServices } from '../../data/outsideYourHome';
import { theLineHeading, howItWorks, managedForYou, theLineBody } from '../../data/brand-lines';
import { localBusiness } from '../../data/business';
import { z } from 'astro/zod';
import { getPage } from '../../lib/cms';
import * as section from '../../lib/cms-schemas';
import { sized } from '../../lib/cms-schemas';

// §0 Metadata. "Pressure washing" and "pressure cleaning" are the same thing
// and are carried in body copy, so the three do not read as three services.
// The description says "for your home" on purpose: with the region gone it is
// now the one signal keeping this result apart from the commercial twin's.
//
// Title and description are the SIGNED-OFF workbook text (Keyword Mapping &
// Metadata, sheet 1 row 16), reproduced verbatim. The old title stopped one
// word short of the mapped primary `high pressure cleaning services` (250/mo);
// the old description ran to 188 characters, so the last fifth including "at a
// pressure the surface can take" — the page's entire differentiator — was
// being truncated in the result.
//
// In `pageMeta`, on `canonical`:
// ⚠️ Placeholder domain, same as every sibling page. Confirm before launch.

// The page's one primary CTA, per BFD 9.5, repeated on every in-page button.
// The approved workbook CTA is the full sentence `Get a fixed quote for your
// home today`, which at 37 characters is a sentence rather than a button
// label: per Rule 4 the sentence goes in the closing block's lead-in and the
// button takes its imperative core. Both come from the same approved text.
//
// ⚠️ NOT BLOCKING, raised for the workbook owner: "fixed" promises a firm
// number and "today" promises same day, on work this page prices from
// photographs — §11's own pricing block says "we'll come back with a number
// quickly" and the FAQs say an old oil stain may not lift at all. Suggested
// replacement: `Get a fast quote for your home today`, one word changed, which
// matches the page's own pricing line and the rest of the site.
//
// The header keeps the site-wide quoteCta — that is chrome, not this page.

// §1 Hero. The H1 now carries the mapped primary `high pressure cleaning
// services` (250/mo) as an exact contiguous phrase, extended with the region:
// local intent on this row totals 1,120/mo across four terms, more than four
// times the mapped primary itself. The old heading is not lost — it opens the
// lead, which is the only place it works, because it is a sentence about the
// driveway rather than about the service.
//
// The subheading is a NEW line. Its extension is scope rather than the H1's
// region, it matches the approved meta word for word on the surface list, and
// it carries `driveway pressure cleaning` (350/mo) and `patio cleaning
// services` (100/mo) into the heading structure.
//
// Scene photo, family A, square source so the 1/1 box crops nothing.

// §2 Definition. The answer target, and the place the synonyms are settled.
// Paragraph two introduces soft washing, which is the distinction most
// competitor pages in this category get wrong, and it is what keeps this page
// honest when it later says not to blast your render.
//
// In `definitionBody`, on the first paragraph:
// Opens with the mapped primary as a contiguous phrase — the opening
// paragraph is scored on the first two sentences. The fourth sentence keeps
// `high pressure cleaning` as a variant, so nothing is given up for it.

// §3 Pathway cards. Three ways people arrive, in their words. Persona cards
// suit this page where they did not suit gutters, because the three jobs here
// really are different purchases: a rescue, a pre-event tidy up and an
// ongoing arrangement.
//
// In `pathwayCards`, on the photo of "It has gone green and slippery":
// No person in this frame on purpose: the subject is the line down
// the middle of the paving, and a figure would compete with it.
// In `pathwayCards`, on the photo of "I want it to just stay done":
// A visible, friendly face, because the copy beside it promises the
// same small team.
// In `pathwayCards`, on the description of "I want it to just stay done":
// ⚠️ [insured] inherited from the commercial hub.

// §4 The warning, placed EARLY on this page rather than late. Every other page
// in this group argues its warning after the scope of work; here the reader
// arrives already wanting force applied to their house, and the honest thing
// is to say what that ruins before describing the job.
//
// `Callout` `warning` tone, used once.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFY THE WORDING. Each item is a well established failure mode:
// pressure etching concrete, washing jointing sand out of pavers, furring and
// splintering softwood decking, stripping render and paint, and forcing water
// behind cladding. No pressure figures and no brand names, both of which
// date. If TLB wants a source, the tile, render and decking manufacturers'
// own care guidance is the honest one to cite.

// §5 Scope of work. `ServiceBlocks` icon grid. Six stages in the order they
// happen. Structurally the same block as the commercial twin's, because the
// method genuinely is the same method, with the items rewritten for a house:
// no trading hours, no WHS duty, no bin bay, and the last one is about your
// garden rather than a stormwater offence.
//
// ⚠️ EVERY ITEM IS DRAFTED against ordinary practice, not supplied by TLB.
// Confirm each and cut what TLB does not do. Two carry blockers, marked.
//
// In `scopeItems`, on "Pre-treat, then clean":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. Confirm hot or cold water. See the file header.
// In `scopeItems`, on "Your garden, your pool, your drain":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER, and the one to get right before publishing.

// §6 What we clean. A plain list rather than `TagCloud`, which is this
// library's pill band and needs an href per pill: every surface here is a
// surface, not a page, and inventing eleven destinations for them would be
// link padding. `TextBlock`'s polymorphic `body` handles a lead-in, a list
// and a conclusion in source order, which is exactly this shape.

// §7 Before and after. SAMPLE illustrations, not photographs. See the window
// page's §6 note, which applies verbatim.
//
// THE PHOTO BRIEF for a real pair, and this is the category where it is most
// worth doing: one driveway, shot from a fixed tripod position, before and
// after, with NOTHING moved between the frames. No car in the second shot, no
// bin shifted, same time of day so the shadows match. Concrete and pavers are
// the best subjects because the change is unmistakable.

// §8 The rest of the cluster. Shared data, this page's own href filtered out.
// The commercial twin is linked separately, in the closing block below, so it
// does not sit in a row of residential services as though it were one.
const siblingItems = otherOutsideServices('/house-cleaning/pressure-cleaning/');

// §9 Comparison table. Shared rows from src/data/comparison.ts.
//
// ⚠️ CONDITIONAL. Row one is "employed by TLB, not subcontracted". If pressure
// cleaning is subcontracted to an operator with the plant, this table
// contradicts the page and comes off it. Same blocker as the commercial twin.

// §11 Branded FAQs, in the customer's voice. Self-contained 40 to 80 word
// answers, per BFD 3.5.
//
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on "What do you need from us on the day?":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. See the file header.

// §12 Non-branded FAQs.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFICATION PASS REQUIRED:
//   - Concrete etching under a held wand, jointing sand washing out of
//     pavers, timber furring and render stripping are all standard and
//     correct.
//   - Algae on shaded paving being a real slip hazard is uncontroversial.
//   - The stormwater answer is correct in substance for NSW: allowing
//     polluting matter to enter stormwater is an offence under the Protection
//     of the Environment Operations Act 1997, and stormwater is untreated. It
//     is worded as a duty, names no section number and no penalty figure, and
//     is SILENT ON QLD, which matters because this service crosses the border.
//     ⚠️ ADD A QLD CLAUSE, or confirm the service area for this page.
//   - Frequency is an observation, hedged.
//   - Pricing bracketed on purpose.
//
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on "Can high pressure cleaning damage a timber deck?":
// ⚠️ BLOCKER. Confirm whether TLB takes deck work at all.
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on "Where is the water allowed to go?":
// ⚠️ SILENT ON QLD. See the note above this array.
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on "How much does high pressure cleaning cost?":
// ⚠️ BRACKETED ON PURPOSE.

// §13 Closing CTA. The commercial twin is linked in the lead rather than as a
// second button, so a business reader who landed here has a way out without
// competing with the page's one CTA (BFD 2.4: one primary CTA per page).

// CONTENT lives in src/content/pages/house-cleaning/pressure-cleaning.yaml and
// is edited in Pages CMS ("High pressure cleaning"). This file owns the layout.
// The notes above explain why each section says what it says; they stay here
// because Pages CMS rewrites the YAML on save and would drop them.
const page = await getPage(
  'house-cleaning/pressure-cleaning',
  z.object({
    seo: section.seo,
    // The text of the page's one primary button. It always links to the
    // site-wide quote page, so only the words are editable.
    buttonLabel: section.text,
    hero: section.hero,
    // Its background photo sits behind the trust bar and this block together
    // (the Backdrop below), so it cannot be left empty.
    definition: section.textBlock.extend({ backgroundImage: section.backgroundPhoto }),
    // A card whose button is left empty gets the page's primary button.
    pathways: section.pathwayCards.extend({
      cards: z.array(section.pathwayCards.shape.cards.element.extend({ cta: section.optional(section.link) })).min(1),
    }),
    warning: section.callout,
    method: section.iconGrid,
    beforeAfter: section.beforeAfter,
    surfaces: section.textBlock,
    // The rows are the shared outside-your-home cross-links.
    otherServices: section.sectionIntro,
    // The columns and rows are the shared comparison table (Site settings).
    comparison: section.comparisonTable.omit({ columns: true, rows: true }),
    reviews: section.sectionHeading,
    whereWeClean: section.tagCloud,
    bookingFaq: section.faq,
    generalFaq: section.faq,
    // The lead ends with the approved workbook CTA sentence, "Get a fixed
    // quote for your home today." (see the primary CTA note above).
    closingCta: section.callToAction,
  }),
);

const pageMeta = {
  ...page.seo,
  canonical: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/house-cleaning/pressure-cleaning/',
};

const business = localBusiness({
  description: pageMeta.description,
  areaServed: 'Northern Rivers NSW, the Tweed and Southern Gold Coast QLD',
  sameAs: googleBusinessProfileUrl ? [googleBusinessProfileUrl] : [],
});

const pageCta = { ...quoteCta, label: page.buttonLabel };

const heroImage = page.hero.image && sized(page.hero.image, '1/1');

const pathwayCards = page.pathways.cards.map((card, i) => ({
  number: i + 1,
  ...card,
  image: sized(card.image, '4/3'),
  cta: card.cta ?? pageCta,
}));

---

<Base title={pageMeta.title} description={pageMeta.description} canonical={pageMeta.canonical} business={business}>
  <SiteHeader
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: logoImg }}
    primaryNav={primaryNav}
    serviceNav={headerNav}
    secondaryCta={headerSecondaryCta}
    cta={quoteCta}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <Hero
      variant="split-single-image"
      imagePosition="left"
      kicker={page.hero.kicker}
      headingLines={page.hero.headingLines}
      subheading={page.hero.subheading}
      lead={page.hero.lead}
      cta={page.hero.cta ?? pageCta}
      image={heroImage}
    />

    <Backdrop image={page.definition.backgroundImage} tint="muted" opacity={90} focus="bottom">
      <TrustBar variant="card" cards={trustBarCards} />
      <TextBlock
        theme="muted"
        align="left"
        heading={page.definition.heading}
        body={page.definition.body}
        cta={page.definition.cta}
      />
    </Backdrop>

    <PathwayCards heading={page.pathways.heading} headingAccent={page.pathways.headingAccent} cards={pathwayCards} />

    {/* The warning sits BEFORE the scope of work on this page, which is the
        reverse of its siblings. See the §4 comment. */}
    <Callout tone="warning" heading={page.warning.heading} body={page.warning.body} cta={page.warning.cta} />

    {/* 🔑 The keyword H2. Third exact instance of `high pressure cleaning
        services`, after the H1 and the hero subheading, and the ceiling — the
        second FAQ heading below keeps `high pressure cleaning` without the
        word that would make it a fourth. Its extension is process, and "stage
        by stage" describes the six items beneath it accurately. */}
    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="icon-grid"
      heading={page.method.heading}
      lead={page.method.lead}
      items={page.method.items}
      cta={page.method.cta ?? pageCta}
    />

    <BeforeAfter
      heading={page.beforeAfter.heading}
      lead={page.beforeAfter.lead}
      pairs={page.beforeAfter.pairs}
      note={page.beforeAfter.note}
      beforeLabel={page.beforeAfter.beforeLabel}
      afterLabel={page.beforeAfter.afterLabel}
    />

    <TextBlock
      theme="dark"
      align="left"
      heading={page.surfaces.heading}
      body={page.surfaces.body}
      cta={page.surfaces.cta}
      backgroundImage={page.surfaces.backgroundImage}
    />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="list"
      heading={page.otherServices.heading}
      lead={page.otherServices.lead}
      items={siblingItems}
    />

    <ComparisonTable
      heading={page.comparison.heading}
      cornerLabel={page.comparison.cornerLabel}
      lead={page.comparison.lead}
      columns={comparisonColumns}
      rows={comparisonRows}
      footnote={page.comparison.footnote}
      cta={page.comparison.cta}
    />

    <GoogleReviewSlider heading={page.reviews.heading} reviews={googleReviews} profileUrl={googleBusinessProfileUrl} />

    <TagCloud
      heading={page.whereWeClean.heading}
      subheading={page.whereWeClean.subheading}
      tags={page.whereWeClean.tags}
      groups={locationGroups}
      note={page.whereWeClean.note}
    />

    {/* §1.3 The Line as a section heading, with §1.4 as its standfirst.
        The copy, and the reason this page gets `fast` rather than the other
        variant, both live in data/brand-lines.ts. Change it there, not here.

        `muted`, not `dark`: TagCloud above paints --color-brand and Faq below
        paints --color-surface, so Cream between them keeps the page
        alternating instead of stacking two dark bands.

        No CTA prop. §9.5 wants one primary CTA per page, repeated, and the
        closing CallToAction is directly under the FAQs. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="muted"
      align="left"
      heading={theLineHeading.fast}
      body={[managedForYou.oneOff, ...theLineBody.residential, ...howItWorks.general]}
    />

    {/* The first FAQ heading names what its five questions actually are —
        damage, oil stains, duration, the day itself and working while you are
        out — all pre-booking questions, and it picks up `driveway pressure
        cleaning` (350/mo) and `patio cleaning services` (100/mo) on the way.
        The second stays: it carries `high pressure cleaning` as a phrase and
        is not a fourth instance of the mapped primary, because it does not
        contain "services". */}
    <Faq heading={page.bookingFaq.heading} lead={page.bookingFaq.lead} items={page.bookingFaq.items} />
    <Faq heading={page.generalFaq.heading} lead={page.generalFaq.lead} items={page.generalFaq.items} />

    <CallToAction
      variant="secondary"
      kicker={page.closingCta.kicker}
      heading={page.closingCta.heading}
      lead={page.closingCta.lead}
      cta={page.closingCta.cta ?? pageCta}
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: footerLogoImg }}
    columns={[
      { title: 'Services', links: footerServiceLinks },
      { title: 'Locations', links: [{ label: 'View all locations', href: '/locations/' }] },
    ]}
    contact={footerContact}
    copyright={footerCopyright}
  />
</Base>
